{"id":"HKF-062","kind":"outcome","key":"Q02","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Observed metric: per-device energy reduction; printed literals: up to 90% (NN), up to 85% (HRE), 81% (LO) in homogeneous battery (Fig. 4a); up to 91% (NN), 85% (HRE), 82% (LO) in heterogeneous battery (Fig. 4b); 10 UAVs.","evidence":[{"page":7,"section":"4.2. Simulation results","quote":"reduces up to 90% in energy over NN,"},{"page":7,"section":"4.2. Simulation results","quote":"reduces up to 91% in energy over NN,"}],"note":""}
{"id":"HKF-062","kind":"outcome","key":"Q03","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Observed metric: end-to-end latency reduction; printed literals: up to 88% vs NN and HRE, and up to 77% vs LO; method: proposed policy; conditions: 10 UAVs in 100 m^2 deployment area (Fig. 3a).","evidence":[{"page":7,"section":"4.2. Simulation results","quote":"improve the performance up to 88% compared to"}],"note":""}
